Whisper: no telemetry, health report or Normandy, at build time

What: builds without the health report service and without Normandy (studies), always
builds Glean with uploads disabled, and makes legacy Telemetry never record. Nimbus
(experiments) counts as disabled for Firefox Labs too.
Why: Whisper does not report on its users. The mozconfig already leaves
MOZ_TELEMETRY_REPORTING unset and the crash reporter out, and 0-whisper.js locks the
prefs off; this removes the code paths too, so no pref can turn them back on.
Normandy is what starts Nimbus; without it Nimbus never initializes, and anything
that waits for it while Nimbus counts as enabled (the new tab page does) waits for
ever. With Labs off as well, Nimbus is disabled outright and those waits end at once.
Adapted from: LibreWolf's disable-data-reporting-at-compile-time.patch (MPL-2.0),
without its edits to the vendored glean-core crate.
---
diff --git a/browser/moz.configure b/browser/moz.configure
index 055df85e58..2695b0d9a8 100644
--- a/browser/moz.configure
+++ b/browser/moz.configure
@@ -3,11 +3,11 @@
 # file, You can obtain one at http://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/.
 
 imply_option("MOZ_PLACES", True)
-imply_option("MOZ_SERVICES_HEALTHREPORT", True)
+imply_option("MOZ_SERVICES_HEALTHREPORT", False)
 imply_option("MOZ_SERVICES_SYNC", True)
 imply_option("MOZ_DEDICATED_PROFILES", True)
 imply_option("MOZ_BLOCK_PROFILE_DOWNGRADE", True)
-imply_option("MOZ_NORMANDY", True)
+imply_option("MOZ_NORMANDY", False)
 imply_option("MOZ_PROFILE_MIGRATOR", True)
 
 
diff --git a/toolkit/components/nimbus/ExperimentAPI.sys.mjs b/toolkit/components/nimbus/ExperimentAPI.sys.mjs
index 282c342ecc..09a4a63769 100644
--- a/toolkit/components/nimbus/ExperimentAPI.sys.mjs
+++ b/toolkit/components/nimbus/ExperimentAPI.sys.mjs
@@ -505,7 +505,8 @@ export const ExperimentAPI = new (class {
   }
 
   get labsEnabled() {
-    return Services.policies.isAllowed("FirefoxLabs");
+    // Whisper: no Nimbus at all (Normandy, which starts it, is not built).
+    return false && Services.policies.isAllowed("FirefoxLabs");
   }
 
   get rolloutsEnabled() {
